Chapter 10 — “The Land of the Lion King”

Chapter 10, Part 37 — “The Executor”

“――G-ghaaah!”

The instant he pulled the knife embedded in his side free, lightning raced through his brain.

His vision turned bright red. He forgot how to breathe in and how to breathe out, while his innards writhed in agony――but that lasted only a few seconds. Immediately afterward, following the commands of his brain as it recovered, he exhaled one long, deep breath.

By the skin of his teeth, barely――he had managed to survive――

“Good, just like the plan――!”

“I’m not going to let you die, but how about you just die?”

Felix’s curse came from right beside Subaru’s ear, whispered at point-blank range. Still, Subaru knew full well that he deserved Felix’s anger; he had done something recklessly insane.

In fact, Subaru’s near-death experience aside, Felix’s current condition was pretty horrific too.――After all, he had lost both arms from the elbows down, and yet he had still prioritized treating Subaru. Felix’s severed arms, which had gotten in the way of that treatment, were still pinned to the wall with a pair of hedge shears.

Honestly, from a tactical standpoint, Subaru had envisioned a somewhat cleaner rescue――

“――The fact that Felix’s arms were pinned down, and the arrival of additional enemies, were both unexpected. I mean, for me, this was supposed to be a zero-risk, safe-bet operation.”

“Where was the ‘safe’ part? You and White Ram-chan nearly died!”

“But you’re here, right? So I figured we had a hundred percent chance of pulling it off.”

“……I’m not Reinhard, you know.”

“――? I’m not Reinhard either, though? That’s what I mean when I say we’re both going to have a hard time.”

Facing Felix, who possessed the ultimate trump card of healing magic, Subaru had rather boldly stretched the meaning of “both.” Still, there was no point wishing for cards he didn’t have. Subaru could only make use of whatever cards were actually in his hand.

For the moment――

“――Miss Crusch, Melty-chan!”

“Please!”

Just like Subaru, Melty, who had been stabbed, urgently needed treatment.

As Subaru shouted, wincing from the healing wound in his side, Crusch responded by generating a gust of wind with magic and gently tossing the fallen Melty through the air.

While carrying Felix on his back, Subaru――

“――Invisible Providence.”

――used the newly manifested third arm to somehow catch the airborne Melty.

Her abdominal wound from the stabbing looked painful, but when she saw Subaru holding her, she――

“……The operation was a success.”

“Yeah. You deserve the Best Actress award.――Felix!”

“You don’t have to tell me, you stupid idiots!”

Despite her pain, Melty smiled bravely, and Subaru gave her a thumbs-up.

As he held Melty, Subaru watched Felix begin treating her wound. At the same time, he once again laid out the cards he could play in this situation.

“――Cor Leonis, back on and full throttle!”

It was the reactivation of an Authority that had been interrupted because Subaru had been ninety-five percent dead.

The effect of “The Little King,” which took on the burdens of his comrades, resumed. As a result, Subaru alone took on the unstoppable emotional “Rupture”――the supernatural ability Bellaris had called the “Ring Finger.”

――No, Felix was here. The burden he had to shoulder wasn’t limited to that.

“――Kgh…”

“――Huh!? Hey, what did you do!? I nearly died again all of a sudden!”

“J-just the damage from two people got piled onto me……yep, woohoo……!”

It hurt. It was agonizing. But the operation had gone well, so he was ultrahappy.

Those negative and positive emotions mixed together inside Subaru, and despite being in the middle of treatment for serious injuries, he was seized by an urge to jump for joy. Should he just give in and start jumping? Both Melty in his arms and Felix on his back felt lighter by exactly the amount of blood they had lost. He could probably bounce around while carrying them both.

“……Are you taking on the abnormalities affecting Lady Crusch and the others? I don’t know how you’re doing it, but……is this some kind of stupid magic you made with Beatrice-chan?”

“Stupid? No way……Beako’s creativity is always pretty-tastic――”

“Shut up! Just keep quiet!――I’ll fix that, too, right now.”

As Subaru was tossed around by the jumble of emotions, Felix rested his chin on Subaru’s shoulder from behind and closed his eyes. He seriously began what was probably a mana-based examination.

It felt like an outrageous maneuver: while simultaneously treating the serious injuries of Subaru and Melty, Felix was also trying to identify the cause of another illness. But if it was Felix, Subaru could only expect him to pull it off.

And while leaving the duplicated “Ring Finger” burden in Felix’s hands――

“――Miss Crusch! Fire!”

Subaru cheered on Crusch, who continued moving nimbly to keep the enemies away from them.

Apparently having joined them through the hole in the underground ceiling, Crusch was engaged in a fierce sword fight with the man wielding hedge shears――Reborn, was it? That was what the enemy had been called.

Naturally, until moments ago, Crusch herself should have been suffering from the corrosion of her mind by the explosion of emotions――

“Yes, Lord Subaru!”

Crusch said this as she swung her sword, and there was a composure about her that was like a tightly stretched thread finally relaxing.

Honestly, the change caught Subaru off guard. His concern, along with his curiosity about what had happened, both threatened to rear their heads at once, but he somehow forcibly suppressed them.

Regardless, the change that had occurred in Crusch was giving her positive strength right now.

The proof was――

“――Hah! Seaaah!”

Crusch stepped forward sharply and cut in. Reborn received the blow with his hedge shears, but the impact sent his small body flying backward.

The enemy spun through the air, planted his soles against the wall at the point where he was flying, and braked his movement――only for a succession of blades of wind to assault him.

With precise aim and rapid-fire speed, the outrageously powerful wind blades were relentlessly hammered into their target.

Even accounting for Crusch’s swordsmanship and the efficiency granted by the “Wind Whisperer’s Divine Protection,” her ability to dominate a battlefield about the size of this underground chamber was in a league of its own.

Including the temporary combat boost granted by the “Dragon’s Eye,” she was easily among the stronger fighters Subaru knew.

Overwhelmed by an attack that was practically a combo with no way out, even this opponent seemed to have his position reversed――

“――Like hell I’ll leeeet you!”

“――!”

Along with a roar, something shot through the barrage of wind blades――a rapidly spinning silver disk.

――No, it was the thrown hedge shears.

Crusch defended against the powerful blow approaching her head-on with an upward slash.

But Reborn slipped into the gap created when the barrage of wind blades stopped. He kicked off the wall, soared through the air, caught his deflected weapon, and enlarged the hole in the ceiling even further――causing a rain of rubble to fall.

Silently.

“Bad――!”

The soundless collapse was like a nightmare that had been delivered without anyone remembering to add the realism.

Despite an utterly ridiculous mass of material falling like a building collapsing in a major earthquake, there was no sense of its significance reaching Subaru. It almost felt as though reality itself was making a mockery of them.

“――――”

The enormous mass of ceiling falling toward them could not be intercepted with blades of wind.

Crusch swiftly dodged the meteor shower of debris, but once her figure disappeared behind the thick cloud of dust billowing upward, Subaru became unbearably anxious about whether she was safe.

Because he was taking on her burden as well, the doubled expansion of his emotions nearly made Subaru burst into tears and scream right there――

“Something like that isn’t enough to do anything to Lady Crusch! Don’t underestimate her!――And that goes for you too, Subaru-kun!”

“――Oh.”

Immediately after being told that, the enormous amount of tears that had welled up all the way behind his eyeballs hastily receded.

The wave of emotional explosion that he had thought unbearable subsided, and a short breath escaped from deep within his throat.

It was freedom from Bellaris’s “poison” that had been eating away at Subaru.

And just as Felix had declared after successfully outwitting the “Ring Finger,” his lord, who had disappeared beyond the cloud of dust, was not so fragile that falling debris could crush her.

“――――”

A soundless leap broke through the smoke screen. Crusch emerged, using the falling rubble as footholds and kicking off each piece, gaining altitude toward the ceiling as though the scene were playing in reverse.

Reborn had driven his hedge shears into the ceiling and was crawling upside down like a gecko. Using the silence, Crusch approached him along a trajectory designed to attack from his blind spot.

Then, for the final kick that would carry her to Reborn――Crusch sprang forward with enough force to blast away a huge piece of debris.

The sound of that kick rang loudly through the silence.

Naturally, that sound told Reborn that she was approaching from his blind spot――

“――Bellaris! Burn it!”

The moment that command flew, the voice of Bellaris――the “Ring Finger” who had disappeared beneath the falling debris and might even have been crushed――came from deep within the dust.

It was a sultry voice filled with heat, as though singing of joy and affection――

“It’s dangerous when things that shouldn’t touch each other end up touching, isn’t it?――That’s what makes it good!”

In an instant, Crusch, who should have been approaching Reborn in midair, swung her sword well before reaching him.

It was not a blade of wind.

It was a magic-slashing technique intended to cancel the enemy’s attack.

A divine technique made possible by the “Dragon’s Eye,” cutting away the signs of magic before activation and preventing it from coming into existence.

That should have stopped the phenomenon occurring between Crusch and Reborn――but the hostility that should have been severed remained intact, and colorful flames blossomed overhead.

Silently.

“Wha――”

To Subaru’s eyes, Crusch’s magic slash had looked perfect.

Yet while her swordsmanship had completely sealed the “Black Dog’s” magic, it could not stop Bellaris’s bizarrely colorful flames――not red, but blue, green, purple, and gold, like fireworks.

“Thiiis is the eeeend――!!”

Crusch was blown away and fell through the air from the resulting blast. Conversely, Reborn added that same wind to his own jumping power and caught up with her.

The hedge shears were raised high, rushing toward Crusch’s slender waist with the intention of cutting her in half.

Other than Reborn’s shout, it was like watching an action scene with the audio muted――an unreal spectacle.

Subaru’s thoughts began to heat up, spinning rapidly.

“――――”

The cards should already have been assembled.

――If he remembered what Melty had told him, each of the “Beloved Children” possessed one ability. “Silence” and “Detour” were easy enough to understand, but only Bellaris’s “Ring Finger” had displayed such an unusual power.

It couldn’t simply be explained as an ability to remove emotional restraint.

That power had a different character from the Authority of the Sin Archbishop of Wrath, but there had to be an explanation that also accounted for the power that had just caused that explosion.

The explosion had not been magic. There had been absolutely no preparation required for it.

If anything, the phenomenon resembled the activation of a trap, and Reborn himself had seemed to know what was going to happen.

There had to be a logical explanation.

There had to be an answer.

Think, think, think.

Apply, apply, apply.

Pursue, pursue, pursue.

See through, see through, see through――

“――!”

His eyes became bloodshot, and at the same time he felt a fierce dryness in his mouth, something brushed against his nostrils.

A faint smell reached Subaru’s nose――a foul odor like rotten eggs.

The reason Subaru recognized what was producing that smell was thanks to the fact that, back when he was in compulsory education, he had been a kid who absolutely loved experiments.

“Miss Crusch! Don’t slash it――make wind!”

How much time had passed while he devoted himself to thinking before he shouted that?

Before he knew it, Reborn was just moments away from catching up to Crusch in midair.

Reborn’s blade was about to reach Crusch――and then, at the very last instant, wind blew.

It was probably a reflexive reaction. Crusch herself likely hadn’t consciously thought about what she was doing.

Wind emerged from the hand opposite the one holding her sword. It raged without a particular target, sending air in the direction of Reborn, who happened to be flying toward her――and there, a golden-yellow explosion erupted.

“Gwaaah――!”

Caught directly in the unexpected explosion, Reborn was sent tumbling across the floor.

Watching him fall, Subaru unconsciously clenched his fist, feeling the certainty that his hypothesis had been correct.

“Amazing…… Subaru-san, how did you――”

“‘Ring Finger,’ huh? The ‘Ring Finger’……What a name!”

Amid the countless explosions blooming in profusion, the foul smell that had reached him was the smell of sulfur.

Having sensed something he hadn’t consciously thought about in a long time, noticed that the flames that had erupted were not limited to red, and combined that with the failure of the magic slash, Subaru had deduced the effect of the “Ring Finger.”

If it had been magic, Crusch would have cut it.

Therefore, it was not magic――

“Bingo! It’s chemistry! A power that scatters substances into the air that absolutely shouldn’t be mixed together!”

Certain drugs enhance the action of chemicals in the brain that switch the human mind and body into a state prepared to fight when confronted with danger.

Bellaris’s supernatural ability produced a similar effect, forcibly putting people into a state of heightened excitement and thereby removing the restraints on their emotions.

As a result, negative emotions became even more negative, while positive emotions likewise became more intense and energetic.

That was the true nature of “Rupture,” and the explosion operated according to the same principle.

Bellaris possessed an ability that produced chemical substances and induced reactions between them to produce whatever effects she desired――

“An elemental chemistry shipper――in other words, despite being like that, she’s a science girl!”

“Rike――jo? Is that my nickname? Giving me a nickname means you love me……? I love you too……!”

“Subaru-kun is the worst. What a cheater.”

“Talk about an unfair reputation!”

After being misunderstood by an unseen enemy hidden within the soot and dust, Subaru was then criticized for it by Felix.

It was an extremely unfavorable situation for Subaru.

And his misfortune continued――

“So you’re the one who figured out all that unnecessary crap……!”

Reborn’s soot-covered face turned toward Subaru after he had been caught in friendly fire.

He had exposed the true nature of the “Ring Finger,” and had also realized that Subaru was the linchpin of their formation.

In an instant, the killing intent of Reborn, who kicked off the floor, was directed toward them.

Subaru instinctively tried to shout out to stop him――

“――Shuuut uuuup!”

“――――”

That single voice sealed away their voices.

Subaru, Felix, and Melty could no longer produce a sound.

In a certain sense, this “Silence” might have been Subaru’s worst possible match.

After all, using words to manipulate his opponents was one of Subaru’s specialty underhanded tactics.

If that were sealed away, he would be practically helpless.

However――

『――Invisible Providence』

This time, Subaru’s voice might have been better off having been heard.

The black arm extending straight from Subaru’s chest headed toward Reborn, who was approaching from the front――

――No.

It headed toward the staircase directly behind Subaru and the others, where they were clustered together, the staircase connecting the underground level with the floors above.

It was the place Subaru had entered the underground and immediately been stabbed by Melty――and there was a door separating the stairwell from the underground chamber.

――The door Melty had closed when they entered and exited.

And this was Kugelschreiber Castle――the former home of Beatrice, where she had once lived together with the “Witch of Greed.”

In other words――

“Huh――?”

Reborn’s crimson eyes widened at the sight beyond the door opened by the black hand.

From beyond that door emerged a masked man who had been sent here from another location within the castle, crossing the intervening space by following the connection of “Cor Leonis” and using “Door Crossing”――

『――Love you, Bea――』

“I won’t leeeet you saaay it!!”

In an unrefined interruption, Reborn cut off the declaration of love from a partner who had reassuringly made his presence known even in a situation like this, and roared, forbidding all sound from conveying any information in this place.

The resulting “Silence” spread throughout the underground chamber.

The sound of Reborn’s approaching footsteps, the breathing and shouts of Subaru and the others, even the first words of the intruder who had appeared――everything became hazily swallowed by the void.

Silently.

But within that “Silence,” Subaru raised his hand high――

“――――”

Without a word, he pointed at Reborn and drew his thumb across his own throat in a gesture.

――The next instant, a green flame was fired without hesitation, swallowing Reborn head-on.

“Gaaaaaaaaah――!”

Cutting straight through the blazing flames with a single stroke, Reborn roared as he broke through the wall of fire and emerged.

His entire body was covered in burns, his eyes blazing with fury as he raised his hedge shears and charged.

A front kick from the “Black Dog,” who had overtaken Subaru and the others, met Reborn’s torso.

A tremendous impact spread without a sound, but the heel stopped against the handle of Reborn’s weapon.

“You’ve done that to me so many ti――Ghoaaah!?”

At that instant, the triumphant face of Reborn was struck by a striking staff swung diagonally across.

It was Melty’s all-out counterattack, having sprung back to her feet.

“Ka――”

With his nose and front teeth broken, Reborn reeled backward and performed a backflip to evade the follow-up attack.

As he fled, the “Black Dog” swept Melty’s legs out from under her, catching her as she fell, but he could not pursue Reborn.

However, Reborn had barely retreated before he was denied even a moment of respite.

“Duke Karsten, Crusch Karsten.”

“You――!”

The voice was the beautiful battlefield introduction of the “Valkyrie,” who stood behind the retreating Reborn, her green hair neatly tied back with a ribbon.

Reborn raised his face as though struck by lightning.

He expanded his “Silence” field and dragged her into his territory.

――But it was a futile resistance.

“――――”

Without needing sound, the wind swept elegantly through the battlefield, and golden eyes traced a path through midair.

The hedge shears raised to intercept her were knocked aside.

With an efficient, graceful movement, the tip of Crusch’s sword danced through the air, approaching Reborn without deviating from its target――

“As expected, Lady Crusch is amazing.”

Just as Felix murmured with deep emotion, the outcome was decided by that single slash.

Both of Reborn’s eyes were cut.

The man covered his face and let out a scream that reverberated throughout the underground chamber.

――It was no longer silence.

His defeat was announced throughout the castle, loudly――loudly.

△▼△▼△▼△

“Kuahahahaha! Looks like you guys got pretty thoroughly beaten up! Covered in blood and all battered, and one of you even lost both hands! There’s a limit to how forgetful you can be!”

“P-please don’t put it like that, ‘Black Dog’! Subaru-san and ‘Blue Snake’-san, and even ‘Verdant Beauty’――everyone was fighting for their lives……!”

“You’re fine, Melty-chan. Don’t worry. He’s probably just embarrassed. He got himself beaten because he was careless, so he arrived late to the important part.”

Subaru shrugged at Melty, who had protested.

Hearing that, the “Black Dog” gave a suspicious, “Melty――?”

He changed the mask on his face to one with an angry expression, then looked back and forth between Subaru and Melty.

“What’s this? You two seem awfully friendly. You even gave him your name, Melty. Did you cozy up to him while I was gone? You wicked woman!”

“W-wicked woman? I’m not――!”

“I told you, knock it off! We just won by working together so well that we could communicate without words. You reacted perfectly, ‘Black Dog.’”

“Kuahaha! Pure coincidence! Your cute and beloved little brat had already told me what to do! Otherwise, how could I possibly respond to ‘come through the door and save the day’ without knowing what was going on?!”

“……Yeah. I owe Beako big-time for that.”

Presumably, even while treating the “Black Dog,” Beatrice had remained constantly conscious of the connection established by her contract with Subaru, preparing herself so that she could respond immediately if he sent any sort of signal.

Thanks to that, immediately after being brought back from the brink of death by Felix, Subaru had used “Cor Leonis” to send reinforcements through the castle, whose “Detour” had been undone, using the nostalgic “Door Crossing.”

“You really saved us.……When our fighting among ourselves had reduced our combat strength to pieces, I had no idea what was going to happen.”

“――Hearing you say that only makes me more ashamed of my own fault.”

Crusch lowered her eyes as she said this, and Subaru faltered.

There was something demure and ladylike about Crusch’s demeanor.

It was different from the steadfast, no-nonsense Crusch Karsten she had displayed over the past two months.

――Subaru had been almost dead, so he had not been able to understand the details, but apparently this was not something that had only started now.

In other words, Subaru had thought that the Crusch Karsten who existed before her “memory” was stolen had returned.

Apparently, however, she had merely been playing that role.

And the reason for that was probably――

“――Lady Crusch, you’re injured. Please allow me to treat you.”

Felix offered to treat Crusch after her fierce battle.

There had presumably been a reason of her own behind the way Crusch had behaved toward him.

Felix surely understood that, yet he did not touch upon it.

Crusch furrowed her brow at that, but more than anything, she was overwhelmed by the state Felix was in.

“You――! Your arms, more than my injuries……! We have to reattach them immediately!”

“Please don’t rush, Lady Crusch. You’re the one who cut them off, you know?”

“That’s exactly why I’m saying this! The cuts should be clean enough, but can they be reattached!?”

Since Felix had deliberately put treating them off, there must have been a way to repair them later.

But Felix did not explicitly say so, instead allowing Crusch to worry herself into a frenzy.

There was something about them that was not quite back to normal yet, but Subaru felt a trace of the atmosphere those two had once shared――at least something close to what they had in Pristella.

But then――

“……What’re you two being all buddy-buddy about, huh?”

A voice that seemed to curse them from the depths of the earth poured cold water over the victorious mood.

Subaru and the others whipped around.

There, staggering to his feet and using the hedge shears as a cane, stood Reborn.

His eyes had been slashed, leaving him blind and apparently incapable of fighting any longer.

Yet his expression was twisted by hatred, overflowing with hostility and killing intent.

“Enough already! Stop! We’ve figured out the trick behind your ‘Silence’! You can turn the sounds within your field of vision on and off, right? That’s why you couldn’t erase the voice coming from behind you. Now that your eyes have been destroyed――”

“So what!? I’m not in any position to back down now! Bellaris! Get rid of the pain! Tornel! Quit screwing around and put the ‘Detour’ back up!”

Spitting as he spoke, Reborn violently struck the floor with his hedge shears and shouted orders to his allies.

In fact, Bellaris’s power should have been capable of eliminating pain through adrenaline.

But she did not answer his plea.

Her blood loss and accumulated injuries had apparently left her unconscious――or perhaps dead. She was no longer moving, and had no strength left to fulfill his request.

And the third person, who still had not shown themselves, made no move to respond either.

It was pitiful.

But Reborn was now in a state where all he could do was wait to be finished off.

However, neither the position of a “Beloved Child” nor his own temperament allowed him to surrender.

Even after realizing that he had no support from his allies, Reborn turned his face toward them, tears of blood flowing down it.

“Fine, then. Whatever……I’ll just kill every last one of you――”

“――No. It ends here. You’ve gone far enough. More than far enough.”

――At that moment, a voice was heard.

It belonged to no one who had been underground until then.

“――――”

Before Subaru and the others, who held their breath in astonishment, a shadow dropped down through the enormous hole in the ceiling.

It landed lightly, cutting between Subaru’s group and Reborn.

Protecting the bloodied man behind him, it confronted Subaru and the others.

A slender figure.

A black hat.

At his waist was a curved sword shaped like a crescent moon.

Subaru recognized him.

And not only Subaru――Crusch and Felix surely did as well.

Perhaps Subaru had imagined that they might one day face each other like this.

But he had never imagined that this person would appear here and now, protecting the “Beloved Children.”

The person who appeared was a pastor of the “Divine Dragon Church,” the gentle-looking man who served as Filore’s bodyguard――

“――Tiga.”

“――――”

At the name, the gentle-looking man――Tiga Laureleon――closed one eye and furrowed his brow.

There was no doubt that the name was his own.

So the reason for Tiga’s suspicious expression was not the name.

It was the person who had called him.

“Tiga……?”

Subaru involuntarily held his breath at the sight of Melty, the one who had called Tiga’s name.

Melty covered her mouth with both hands and stared at Tiga with her large, round eyes.

In those eyes was shock――and behind it, a great joy that she could not completely hide.

“――?”

Tiga, on the other hand, seemed to have no idea what was behind Melty’s enormous emotional reaction.

He appeared puzzled by the way she was looking at him.

For an instant, the intrusion of Tiga and the strange atmosphere surrounding it caused an odd silence to fall over the scene.

Then, immediately afterward――

“Tiga, you know that girl, ya?”

A small presence leaned out from Tiga’s shoulder as it spoke.

――It was a squirrel-like spirit with a cute yet cheeky face and a curled tail.

Tiga, accompanied by the unfamiliar spirit, shook his head at her question.

“No.”

He paused.

“She should be someone I don’t know.”

“――!”

“But she sure looks like she knows you, ya. And……there’s no mistaking it. That big, weirdly dressed one over there.――That’s my contractor.”

“Huh!? What the hell is that tiny little spirit talking about!?”

Melty’s expression clouded at Tiga’s answer, while the “Black Dog” reacted angrily to the spirit’s words.

There were all sorts of unexplained lines being drawn between the people present.

But the one who could no longer tolerate the situation was not Subaru and the others.

It was Reborn, the person being protected.

“You――‘Executor’! What the hell are you doing!? This was supposed to be our――”

“――Time’s up. The situation has changed. I wasn’t planning on rushing in here either. But when you guys started making that much noise――”

“‘Making that much noise’? Mind telling us what happened, my friend?”

Subaru interrupted his conversation with Reborn.

At the sarcastic address of “my friend,” Tiga slightly raised an eyebrow.

The corner of Tiga’s mouth twisted.

――There was something almost self-deprecating about the expression, causing Subaru to furrow his brow.

But before Subaru could voice his question, Tiga answered it.

What had happened that was so conspicuous?

The answer was――

“This castle broke out of the alternate space and emerged on this side.――Right now, it’s the center of attention for the entire Kingdom.”

――The news that Kugelschreiber Castle had broken four hundred years of silence and taken to the skies.
